🎯 Deloitte SDE2 (Java) interviews
Compiled these from patterns widely reported by candidates across interview-prep communities. If you're prepping for an SDE2 Java role — not just Deloitte — this list covers what actually gets asked.
𝗥𝗼𝘂𝗻𝗱 𝟭 — 𝗢𝗻𝗹𝗶𝗻𝗲 𝗔𝘀𝘀𝗲𝘀𝘀𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁
 • Find the first non-repeating character in a string
 • Detect a cycle in a linked list
 • MCQs on OOP concepts, exception handling, DBMS normalization, and basic aptitude
𝗥𝗼𝘂𝗻𝗱 𝟮 — 𝗖𝗼𝗿𝗲 𝗝𝗮𝘃𝗮 & 𝗗𝗦𝗔
 • What's the difference between == and .equals()? Why does String behave differently?
 • Why must equals() and hashCode() always be overridden together?
 • How does HashMap work internally? What changed in Java 8?
 • Difference between HashMap, LinkedHashMap and TreeMap?
 • Explain the 4 pillars of OOP — with a real example from your own project
 • Interface vs abstract class — when do you actually choose one over the other?
 • Method overloading vs overriding — what's resolved at compile time vs runtime?
 • Two Sum — find the first pair that adds up to a target
 • What is the diamond problem, and how does Java avoid it?
𝗥𝗼𝘂𝗻𝗱 𝟯 — 𝗦𝗽𝗿𝗶𝗻𝗴, 𝗦𝗤𝗟 & 𝗗𝗲𝘀𝗶𝗴𝗻
 • What is dependency injection, and why constructor injection over field injection?
 • What are Spring's default bean scopes? When would you use something other than singleton?
 • Difference between @Component, @Service, @Repository, @Controller?
 • What is the N+1 query problem in Hibernate/JPA, and how do you fix it?
 • @Transactional — default propagation vs REQUIRES_NEW?
 • What is idempotency, and why does it matter for REST APIs?
 • Design a rate limiter for an API — walk through your approach
 • synchronized vs ReentrantLock — when would you actually reach for Lock?
𝗥𝗼𝘂𝗻𝗱 𝟰 — 𝗠𝗮𝗻𝗮𝗴𝗲𝗿𝗶𝗮𝗹 / 𝗛𝗥
 • Walk me through a challenging bug you fixed
 • Why Deloitte?
 • Tell me about a time you disagreed with a teammate on a technical decision
 • What questions do you have for me?
